claim.claim-text:
receiving, by a first computing device (2A) of a plurality of computing devices (2), each of which are associated with a user and are located in physical proximity to one another, a spoken audio input, wherein the spoken audio input is also received by a second computing device (2B) of the plurality of computing devices (2);
determining, by a negotiation module (40) of the first computing device (2A), a first audio input quality of the spoken audio input received by the first computing device;
sending, by the negotiation module (40) of the first computing device (2A) and to a negotiation module of the second computing device (2B), an indication of the first audio input quality;
receiving, by the negotiation module (40) of the first computing device (2A) and from the negotiation module of the second computing device (2B), an indication of a second audio input quality of the spoken audio input received by the second computing device (2B);
determining, by the negotiation module of the first computing device (2A), and based on a comparison of the first audio input quality and the second audio input quality by the negotiation module (40) of the first computing device (2A), whether the first computing device (2A) should process the spoken audio input; and
responsive to determining that the first computing device (2A) should process the spoken audio input, processing, by the first computing device (2A), the spoken audio input to determine whether the spoken audio input includes a predetermined audio command.

sending, by the negotiation module of the first computing device (2A) and to respective negotiation modules of each other computing device (2C), the indication of the first audio input quality; and
receiving, by the negotiation module of the first computing device (2A) and from the respective negotiation modules of each other computing device (2C), an indication of a respective audio input quality of the spoken audio input received by the respective computing device (2C);
determining, by the negotiation module of the first computing device (2A), and based on a comparison of the first audio input quality and the second audio input quality and the respective audio input qualities by the negotiation module of the first computing device (2A), whether the first computing device (2A) should process the spoken audio input.
